# Line endings.
#
# Prettier writes LF and its `endOfLine` default expects LF, but a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true checks files out as CRLF — so `npm run lint` reported a "Delete ␍" error
# on every line of every file, and the format check could not pass locally even though CI,
# running on Linux, saw nothing wrong. Normalising here makes both agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Lockfiles are generated; a diff of one is noise in review.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated

# Binary assets: never normalise, never diff.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
